LANGUAGE FOCUS   "Value"
English value carries no built-in basis: book value, market value, fair value, net realisable value and present value are five different numbers for one asset, and the word alone tells the reader nothing. Arabic uses قيمة with the same breadth, and French valeur likewise. The professional habit is to name the basis every time. A marker cannot misread an answer written that way.
