Market-to-book | 1.9355: 6.00 ÷ 3.10, where the price comes from 6,000,000 ÷ 1,000,000 = 6.00.
What it tells you | Barada grows about two points a year faster than it can fund, retains everything, and pays no dividend, so the gap can only go on the overdraft. The investor's offer values it at nearly twice book, which is a judgment about the distribution business and not about the balance sheet.
